  "previousGoalTurn": "The latest key-location reply confirmed existing memory without changing implementation (no progress on the broad goal). Revalidated the worktree and continued from C69's committed candidate-selection work.",
  "findings": [
    "Cancellation was first checked after synchronous launch input validation, which hashes both source locks and the executable.",
    "Live verification did not propagate caller cancellation while hashing six artifacts, component receipts and the executable after process exit.",
    "Companion cancellation handling intentionally performs uncancelled read-only terminal reconciliation: a valid committed pass or rejection wins."
  ],
  "implementation": [
    "Check cancellation before launch validation; pass the caller token through all live file-hash paths and bounded receipt reads.",
    "Use a single 1 MiB streaming SHA-256 helper with checks before/after every read, including EOF; preserve short-read behavior, size validation, I/O errors and caller ownership.",
    "Preserve synchronous intent creation, durable reconciliation, public API, identities and terminal evidence."
  ],
